# ISO-only AUR packages (installed via the local [vinos-aur] repo,
# NOT pulled by install/*.sh on installer path).
#
# Format: one package per line, comments and blanks ignored.
# gen-packages.sh merges these into both packages.x86_64 (so mkarchiso
# pacstraps them from vinos-aur) and aur.list (so aur-build.sh knows
# to build them).
#
# NOTE: T2 Mac support packages (linux-t2, apple-bcm-firmware,
# apple-t2-audio-config, tiny-dfr, t2fanrd) are NOT AUR — they live
# in the community [arch-mact2] pacman repo (see iso/profile/pacman.conf
# + iso/packages.live). Do NOT add them here.

# walker's new 2.16+ architecture split "elephant" into a separate
# AUR package that walker-bin depends on at runtime. aur-build.sh
# builds elephant first (alphabetical order) and pushes it into
# [vinos-aur] so walker-bin's makepkg -s can resolve it.
elephant

# OOBE-parity: vendor DKMS drivers baked into the squashfs. Each builds
# against the shipped `linux` kernel headers at mkarchiso time, so the
# live boot already has the module (no first-boot DKMS wait).
# macbook12-spi-driver-dkms — pre-2018 butterfly-keyboard MBPs (T2 stack
#                             handles 2018+; this covers 2015-2017)
#
# Deferred to install/06-hardware.sh (post-install) because the AUR
# entries are either gone (asdcontrol, dell-xps-touchpad-haptics — no
# PKGBUILD in AUR as of 2026-07) or their upstream source URL 404s
# (yt6801-dkms). 06-hardware.sh already retries with warn-and-continue.
macbook12-spi-driver-dkms

# OOBE-parity: shell-referenced userspace that only lives in AUR.
# xdg-terminal-exec — resolves $TERMINAL / handlr terminal preference
#                     for walker + hyprland keybind that opens a shell.
xdg-terminal-exec

# OOBE-parity: apps bound to keybindings in config/hypr/hyprland.conf.
# Super+M → spotify · Super+/ → 1password · terminal ops → 1password-cli.
# aur-build.sh caches these in iso/.aur-cache so rebuilds are fast (~90 s).
spotify
1password
1password-cli
